Attribution and citation requirement (licence-bound)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Any person or organisation reusing this software, the five-stage
pipeline design, the twelve-relation closed grammar, the deterministic
Sugiyama layout, the frozen Qwen2.5-7B encoder integration, the math
extension (primitives, relations, and KaTeX-rendered inner labels), or
any artefact in the bench/eval/ harness (rubric, gold-set, raw JSON
results, cost ledger) — in research, in derivative software, in
courseware, in commercial evaluation, or in any other form — MUST cite
the SeVim paper using the BibTeX entry above (or, after acceptance, the
venue-specific entry that supersedes it).

The repository is distributed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
The MIT License does NOT formally require citation, but if you build
on this work in a paper, textbook, courseware, or commercial product,
the maintainers would appreciate the BibTeX entry above being included.
Academic citations help the project's research-community footprint and
make future open-source contributions more likely.
